4:["$","p","6",{"data-count":"","children":["On the northeast plain, 40.3 percent of farmers surveyed were over 54 and only 10.6 percent were under the age of 35 ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","huo",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#huo","children":"Huo et al. 2022"}]]}]],")"]}],". In Lishu County in the neighbouring Jilin province (the region with second highest corn production as seen in the choropleth map), the average farmer surveyed was 58 ",["$","span","3",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","yu",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#yu","children":"Yu et al. 2025"}]]}]],")"]}],"."]}]
5:["$","figure","7",{"className":"photo photo-graph photo-narrow","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/graphs/heilongjiang-age-pyramid-2019.png","alt":"Population pyramid of Heilongjiang in 2019 by five-year age group, males in blue on the left and females in red on the right. The widest bars are ages 40 to 54, and the bars for children and young adults are much narrower.","width":480,"height":422,"loading":"lazy","decoding":"async"}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["Heilongjiang’s population by age and sex in 2019, in units of 10,000 people (blue male, red female). The widest bars are people aged 40 to 54, with far fewer children and young adults below them."," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"credit","children":["Graph",": ","Rickky1409",","," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","rel":"license","children":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],", via"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China_Heilongjiang_pop_SbA5y_pyramid2019.png","children":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"."]}]]}]]}]
6:["$","h2","8",{"data-count":"","children":"Do machines replace people?"}]
7:["$","p","9",{"data-count":"","children":["I suggested in the progress check-in that people leave first and machines follow, however a more nuanced story is supported by the major articles and data I’ve seen. The large gently sloping farms are very optimal for machine use, but Northeast Plain farmers ranked a lack of machinery training as the biggest barrier, industrial machines for corn farming cost from US$1,500 to US$15,000 which exposes machinery as an unwise business practice given that farmers earn under US$181.49 per hectare ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","huo",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#huo","children":"Huo et al. 2022"}]]}]],")"]}],". Many hire machine services instead despite the higher cost long term."]}]
8:["$","figure","10",{"className":"photo","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/photos/corn-crib-liaoning.jpg","alt":"Harvested yellow corn cobs stacked behind wire mesh in a metal storage crib","width":1400,"height":1050,"loading":"lazy","decoding":"async"}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":["Harvested corn cobs drying in a family’s storage crib in Gaizhou, Liaoning, in the north-east corn belt, October 2019."," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"credit","children":["Photo",": ","Jason M. C. Han",","," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","rel":"license","children":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],", via"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corns_Harvesting_Storage.jpg","children":"Wikimedia Commons"}],"."]}]]}]]}]
9:["$","p","11",{"data-count":"","children":["Only 54 percent of Lishu farmers had adopted conservation tillage, and some of the others were ‘informed non-adopters’ who understood the cultivation method but had more faith in traditional practices. I think that the ageing, hesitant workforce is the pressure being handled least well."]}]
